    <!-- Section 10: Measuring AI Search Performance -->
    <section>
      <h2>Measuring AI Search Performance</h2>

      <p>Measuring AI search performance is fundamentally different from tracking traditional SEO metrics. There is no equivalent of Google Search Console for AI citations — yet. However, effective measurement is still possible through a combination of manual monitoring and emerging tools.</p>

      <h3>Manual Citation Tracking</h3>

      <p>The most reliable method for tracking AI search visibility is regular manual testing. Run your target queries across ChatGPT, Perplexity, Copilot, and Google (for AIO) and record whether your business is cited. Key queries to monitor for a Birmingham business include:</p>

      <ul>
        <li>Your brand name (e.g., "tell me about [business name] Birmingham")</li>
        <li>Your core service + location (e.g., "best [service] in Birmingham")</li>
        <li>Comparison queries (e.g., "[service A] vs [service B] Birmingham")</li>
        <li>Informational queries in your niche (e.g., "how much does [service] cost in Birmingham")</li>
      </ul>

      <p>Run these tests weekly and log the results. Over time, you will see patterns emerge: which platforms cite you most frequently, which queries you are missing from, and how your visibility changes as you implement optimisation.</p>

      <h3>Emerging Monitoring Tools</h3>

      <p>Several tools are emerging to automate AI search monitoring, including Otterly.ai, HubSpot's AI Search Grader, and custom scripts that query AI APIs and parse responses for brand mentions. While the tooling is still maturing, early adoption gives Birmingham businesses a data advantage over competitors who are not tracking AI visibility at all.</p>

      <h3>KPIs for AI Search</h3>

      <p>Set measurable KPIs for your AI search optimisation programme:</p>

      <ul>
        <li><strong>Citation frequency</strong> — how often your business is mentioned in AI answers for target queries. Track this monthly.</li>
        <li><strong>Citation accuracy</strong> — whether the AI's description of your business is correct. Inaccurate citations can be more damaging than no citation at all.</li>
        <li><strong>Source link inclusion</strong> — whether the AI provides a link to your website alongside the citation. Linked citations drive traffic; unlinked citations drive brand awareness only.</li>
        <li><strong>Competitive share of voice</strong> — how your citation frequency compares to Birmingham competitors for the same queries.</li>
        <li><strong>Referral traffic from AI sources</strong> — check your analytics for traffic from chat.openai.com, perplexity.ai, and bing.com/chat domains.</li>
      </ul>
    </section>

